        "Article 2 The fundamental Aqidah of this organization is: \"La ilaha illallahu Muhammadur Rasulullah.\" That is, there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah.",
        "Explanation (a) The First Part of the Fundamental Aqidah: \"La ilaha illallah\". The statement \"There is no deity except Allah\" means that Allah Almighty alone is the Creator, Sustainer, Owner, the only One worthy of worship, and the Absolute Sovereign over the entire universe. He has no partner, associate, or equal in His Essence, Attributes, or Authority. Every person who sincerely embraces this fundamental belief must wholeheartedly accept the following: 1. No one besides Allah Almighty shall be regarded as one's guardian, disposer of affairs, fulfiller of needs, remover of hardships, hearer and responder of supplications, helper, or protector. 2. One's life, body, mental and physical strength, knowledge, intellect, abilities, and all capacities shall be regarded as belonging to Allah Almighty and entrusted by Him. One shall remain conscious that these trusts must be accounted for before Allah in the Hereafter. 3. One shall adopt what Allah Almighty loves and dislikes as one's own likes and dislikes. In other words, attaining the pleasure and closeness of Allah shall be the ultimate objective of all efforts, actions, and aspirations. 4. In every aspect of life, one shall accept only the guidance revealed by Allah Almighty as the true guidance and reject all laws, ideologies, systems, methods, and practices that contradict the Shariah ordained by Allah.",
