        "Central President or his/her authorized representative. Membership shall become effective from the date the oath is taken.",
        "Duties and Responsibilities of Members",
        "Article 9 Every member of the Korea Muslim Community shall continuously strive to bring about the following changes in his or her life: 1. To give the highest priority to obedience to Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ), and to the observance of their commands and prohibitions. 2. To acquire sufficient knowledge of Islam to distinguish Islam from Jahiliyyah, understand the limits prescribed by Allah through Shariah, and shape one's faith (Iman), beliefs (Aqidah), and entire way of life in accordance with the Qur'an and Sunnah. 3. To align one's life purpose, preferences, loyalties, and all aspects of life with the pleasure of Allah; to avoid self-desire and self-worship; and to submit oneself completely to the commandments of Allah. 4. To perform all activities with consciousness of Allah (Taqwa), sincere obedience to Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ), honesty, and justice. 5. To purify one's heart and life from all forms of Jahili customs, traditions, superstitions, and practices that contradict the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger (ﷺ), as well as matters that have no basis in Islam. 6. Except where required for the sake of the Deen, to refrain from intimate friendship and attachment with those who turn away from Allah, and to establish strong relationships with righteous people. 7. To make every possible effort to spread Islamic teachings and bear witness to the Deen among one's family, relatives, neighbors, and surrounding community; to center all efforts and activities on the establishment of the Deen; and, except for the necessities of life, to refrain from activities that do not contribute toward this objective. 8. To present the Islamic faith (Iman and Aqidah), together with the",
        "objectives, goals, and policies of the Korea Muslim Community, to acquaintances and to all people within one's reach; to encourage those who accept these beliefs and objectives to participate in the collective effort to establish the Deen of Allah; and to invite those who are willing to become members of the Korea Muslim Community.",
